---
import Base from '../layouts/base.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/code-block.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const withBase = (p: string) => (base.endsWith('/') ? base + p : base + '/' + p);

const cssCode = `.my-editor-wrapper {
  --beaket-paper-accent: #0c6bae;     /* links, focus, selection tint */
  --beaket-paper-fg: #232a35;         /* body text + caret */
  --beaket-paper-bg: #fffefc;         /* writing surface (default #fff) */
  --beaket-paper-font: Georgia, serif;
  --beaket-paper-font-size: 16.5px;
  --beaket-paper-measure: 42rem;      /* max line width; default none = full width */
  --beaket-paper-word-break: keep-all; /* Korean: break at spaces, not mid-word; default normal */
}`;
---

<Base title="Styling — Paper">
  <h1>Styling</h1>

  <p>
    The editor ships its own visual tokens via a CodeMirror theme scoped to <code>.cm-editor</code>, so
    it works standalone — no CSS file to import.
  </p>

  <h2 id="tokens">CSS variables</h2>
  <p>
    Every token resolves through <code>var(--beaket-paper-X, …)</code>. Set any of them on
    <code>:root</code> or any ancestor of the editor and it follows — no <code>!important</code>, no
    specificity fights:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={cssCode} lang="css" />
  <p class="callout callout-note">
    <svg class="callout-icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M0 8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z" />
    </svg>
    <span><strong>Note</strong> — <code>letter-spacing</code> is intentionally not exposed: negative spacing breaks mixed-script CJK, so it is fixed at <code>0</code> (a CJK-first guard).</span>
  </p>

  <h3 id="token-list">Color tokens</h3>
  <p>Color tokens are named by role. Each one bridges to the <code>@beaket/ui</code> semantic token of the same role:</p>
  <div class="table-scroll">
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Token</th><th>Bridges to</th><th>Used for</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>--beaket-paper-fg</code></td><td><code>--color-fg</code></td><td>Body text, caret, checked checkbox</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--beaket-paper-fg-muted</code></td><td><code>--color-fg-muted</code></td><td>Blockquotes, list markers, footnote numbers, menu hints</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--beaket-paper-fg-subtle</code></td><td><code>--color-fg-subtle</code></td><td>Syntax markers, image placeholders, table hints</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--beaket-paper-bg</code></td><td><code>--color-bg-input</code></td><td>The writing surface</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--beaket-paper-bg-raised</code></td><td><code>--color-bg-raised</code></td><td>Inline code and code blocks</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--beaket-paper-bg-overlay</code></td><td><code>--color-bg-overlay</code></td><td>Menus, popovers, copy buttons</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--beaket-paper-bg-hover</code></td><td><code>--color-bg-hover</code></td><td>Hovered menu items and table cells</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--beaket-paper-bg-active</code></td><td><code>--color-bg-active</code></td><td>Table row and column grips (active)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--beaket-paper-border-subtle</code></td><td><code>--color-border-subtle</code></td><td>Inline code and button outlines</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--beaket-paper-border</code></td><td><code>--color-border</code></td><td>Menus, tables, rules, images</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--beaket-paper-border-strong</code></td><td><code>--color-border-strong</code></td><td>Unchecked checkbox</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--beaket-paper-accent</code></td><td><code>--color-accent-solid</code></td><td>Links, focus, selection tint</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--beaket-paper-shadow</code></td><td><code>--shadow-offset-overlay</code></td><td>Overlay shadow</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    The code-syntax colors (<code>--beaket-paper-syntax-*</code>) and typography
    (<code>-font</code>, <code>-font-size</code>, <code>-line-height</code>, <code>-measure</code>,
    <code>-word-break</code>) are the editor's own and have no bridge.
  </p>
  <p>
    The earlier names — <code>ink</code>, <code>steel</code>, <code>muted</code>, <code>canvas</code>,
    <code>surface</code>, <code>paper</code>, <code>frost</code>, <code>chrome</code>,
    <code>platinum</code>, <code>silver</code>, <code>slate</code> — still work as deprecated aliases
    through 0.x and are removed at 1.0.
  </p>

  <h2 id="bridge">Design-token bridge</h2>
  <p>
    Inside a <code>@beaket/ui</code> app the editor inherits the theme automatically — including dark
    mode — with no setup. Each color token resolves three tiers deep:
    <code>var(--beaket-paper-ROLE, var(--color-ROLE, default))</code> — your explicit override first,
    then the host's semantic token of the same role, then a built-in default.
  </p>

  <h2 id="dark">Dark mode</h2>
  <p>
    The editor follows the OS <code>prefers-color-scheme</code> automatically — no setup, no class to
    toggle. Every token carries a dark-aware default, so body text, surfaces, and the code-syntax ramp
    all flip together.
  </p>
  <p>
    Theming still wins in both modes: a token you set on <code>:root</code> or an ancestor —
    <code>--beaket-paper-*</code> directly, or the host's <code>--color-*</code> palette through the
    bridge — applies to light and dark alike. To diverge per scheme, set your overrides inside your own
    <code>@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)</code> block.
  </p>

  <h2 id="escape">Escape hatches</h2>
  <p>For anything the variables don't cover:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Style the stable <code>.cm-*</code> class hooks directly — e.g. <code>.cm-table-widget</code>, <code>.cm-slash-menu</code>, <code>.cm-md-copy</code>.</li>
    <li>Reach the underlying CodeMirror <code>EditorView</code> via <code>ref.current.getView()</code> to add your own extensions or theme.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="next"><a href={withBase('')}>← Back to overview</a></p>
</Base>
